          ],
          "type": "systematic_shift",
          "magnitude_years": 100,
          "confidence": "medium",
          "description": "SP and LXX both add 100 to the fathering ages of Arpachshad, Shelah, Eber, Peleg, Reu and Serug (and 50 to Nahor). Steinmann's collation of all 860 Genesis variants finds SP and LXX share 96 secondary readings against 4 (MT+SP) and 2 (MT+LXX), so their agreement here counts as one text type, not two witnesses. He reads the lengthening as a scribal fix for MT's crowded family (on MT with Terah 130: Shem dies AM 2158, after Isaac's birth; Eber dies AM 2187, after Abraham). Contested: Henry B. Smith Jr. (ICC 2018) argues the longer numbers are original.",
          "theological_significance": "Worth about 590 years on the post-Flood chain (on the 1446 BC Exodus anchor: MT Flood 2303 BC; SP chain 2893 BC; LXX without Cainan 2953-3053 BC). No reading moves the Flood clearly before Egypt's First Dynasty (Aha, 3111-3045 BC) except the LXX with the second Cainan. Source: Steinmann, 'A Comparison of the Text of Genesis in Three Traditions', JETS 64/1 (2021) 25-43; see docs/content/chronology/flood-and-the-king-lists.md"
        }
      ],
